shatteredcitadels.lore.1.1=Before kings and before stone there was a design. The Ancient Architects, a people without names, could listen to the world and build from its voice.
shatteredcitadels.lore.1.2=They raised the first citadels not for war but as strings of a great lyre stretched between earth and sky. Every tower sang its own note.
shatteredcitadels.lore.1.3=The last Architect scroll reads: 'We build so the world remembers what it is meant to be.' It breaks off, as if the scribe was called to a council he never returned from.
shatteredcitadels.lore.2.1=Nine Architects fused their voices into one Crown. It did not sit on a head; it held every citadel of the world in balance.
shatteredcitadels.lore.2.2=Whoever wore the Crown heard every tower at once. They say the wearer could order stone to rise as a wall and wind to become a bridge.
shatteredcitadels.lore.2.3=But the voice of nine was too heavy for one. Keepers of the Crown aged a lifetime in a year, and their shadows walked the halls after death.
shatteredcitadels.lore.3.1=The boldest Architects built above the clouds. Their spires touched the sky, and up there the stars were closer than the market at the foot of the tower.
shatteredcitadels.lore.3.2=On the summits they kept shards of celestial fire and learned from storms. The Sky Sovereigns, their students, walked on air as on marble floors.
shatteredcitadels.lore.3.3=If you see a tower above the clouds, know this: its peace is guarded below, and at the top waits one who has forgotten how to walk on the ground.
shatteredcitadels.lore.4.1=On the Night of Shattering the last Keeper chose to wear the Crown himself. Nine voices argued in his head, and the Crown cracked with a sound that silenced the birds.
shatteredcitadels.lore.4.2=The shards scattered across all citadels. Towers robbed of their voice began to call the dead and the monstrous, anything to fill their empty halls.
shatteredcitadels.lore.4.3=Since then every citadel guards its shard behind the Keeper's Arena. Whoever gathers them may hear the world again, or go deaf forever.
shatteredcitadels.lore.5.1=Beneath the deepest citadels the Architects kept forges. Goblins worked them: a small, greedy and endlessly inventive people.
shatteredcitadels.lore.5.2=The goblins forged tools that mended themselves. The Heart of their forge beat like a living thing and fed the fire without coal or air.
shatteredcitadels.lore.5.3=When the Crown shattered, the goblins sealed their forges and went down into the dark. They say their Heart still beats somewhere beneath our feet.
shatteredcitadels.lore.6.1=The dark below the citadels is not empty. Cut off from the sky, the goblins grew bitter, and with them woke what the Architects once buried.
shatteredcitadels.lore.6.2=The crypts under the castles are not graves but prisons. Every trap in their corridors was set not for thieves, but to keep something inside.
shatteredcitadels.lore.6.3=When you descend, hold your torch close and listen to the floor. If it rings hollow under your steps, there is one more level and one more guardian.
shatteredcitadels.lore.7.1=The Crown cannot be mended, but it can be inherited. Each shard knows the one who passed the trials of its citadel and grants them a part of its power.
shatteredcitadels.lore.7.2=The Aegis of the Cloudspire, the Heart of the Goblin Forge, the Architect's Blade: not trophies, but old voices looking for a new listener.
shatteredcitadels.lore.7.3=If you are reading this, the citadels have already chosen you. Climb higher, dig deeper, and remember: the world is built anew whenever someone dares.
